.TH QFW-QPM-SVC 1 "August 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw Commands"
.SH NAME
qfw-qpm-svc \- manage one QFw QPM service instance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qfw-qpm-svc
.I start|run
.B --run-dir
.I path
.B --service-id
.I id
[
.I options
]
.PP
.B qfw-qpm-svc
.I status|stop
.B --run-dir
.I path
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw-qpm-svc
starts, supervises, inspects, or stops exactly one QPM and its optional PRTE
DVM. It reads directory connection information automatically from the site
configuration or from
.BR --directory-service-info .
.PP
In application scope QPMd and the PRTE DVM master run on the head of
allocation group 1. In site scope
.B --node
selects the QPM node. Remote placement requires a Slurm allocation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --run-dir " path"
Private lifecycle state, PID, readiness, DVM URI, and log directory.
.TP
.BI --service-id " id"
The single service manifest entry managed by this instance. The option may be
specified only once.
.TP
.BI --directory-service-info " path"
Override the client-readable directory connection record. Site scope normally
obtains this path from
.BR qfw-site.yaml (5).
.TP
.BI --site-config " path"
Site configuration.
.TP
.BI --runtime-config " path"
Runtime configuration.
.TP
.BI --scope " application|site"
Select application-owned or site-owned lifetime and placement rules.
.TP
.BI --node " node"
Site-scope QPM node. This option is rejected in application scope.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Resolve and record the plan without starting processes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-dir-svc (1),
.BR qfw-site.yaml (5),
.BR qfw-services.yaml (5),
.BR qfw-service-plane (7)
